== 3.11 Chapter 3 Practice Drill — 40 Questions

40 questions graded in the order the CBT engine is likely to meet them. Allow 44 minutes; the key and a full solution for every question follow.

#mcq(1, [The enthalpy change of a reaction is the heat change measured at],
  [constant pressure],
  [constant mass],
  [constant temperature],
  [constant volume]
)

#mcq(2, [In an exothermic reaction, the enthalpy change is],
  [impossible to measure],
  [zero],
  [negative, and the surroundings warm],
  [positive, and the surroundings cool]
)

#mcq(3, [For the reaction H₂(g) + Cl₂(g) → 2HCl(g), ΔH = −183 kJ mol⁻¹. The reaction is],
  [reversible only],
  [neutral],
  [exothermic],
  [endothermic]
)

#mcq(4, [Which quantity is a measure of the energy stored in the bonds of a compound?],
  [lattice energy],
  [ionisation energy],
  [bond enthalpy],
  [activation energy]
)

#mcq(5, [The reaction 2H₂(g) + O₂(g) → 2H₂O(l) has ΔH = −572 kJ. The enthalpy change per mole of water formed is],
  [−143 kJ mol⁻¹],
  [−286 kJ mol⁻¹],
  [−1144 kJ mol⁻¹],
  [−572 kJ mol⁻¹]
)

#mcq(6, [Which of the following is an exothermic process?],
  [dissolving ammonium nitrate],
  [melting ice],
  [condensation of steam],
  [boiling water]
)

#mcq(7, [In an endothermic reaction, the energy of the products is],
  [lower than that of the reactants],
  [equal to that of the reactants],
  [zero],
  [higher than that of the reactants]
)

#mcq(8, [The standard enthalpy of combustion is the enthalpy change when one mole of a substance],
  [is dissolved in water],
  [reacts with oxygen completely, under standard conditions],
  [is formed from its elements],
  [is burned in a bomb]
)

#mcq(9, [The standard enthalpy of formation of an element in its standard state is],
  [negative],
  [zero],
  [undefined],
  [positive]
)

#mcq(10, [Hess's law states that the enthalpy change of a reaction depends only on],
  [the initial and final states],
  [the catalyst used],
  [the route taken],
  [the rate of reaction]
)

#mcq(11, [Which equation correctly represents the standard enthalpy of formation of water?],
  [2H₂(g) + O₂(g) → 2H₂O(l)],
  [H₂O(g) → H₂O(l)],
  [H₂O(l) → H₂(g) + ½O₂(g)],
  [H₂(g) + ½O₂(g) → H₂O(l)]
)

#mcq(12, [A reaction has ΔH = +58 kJ mol⁻¹. This means that],
